Error [jet.ViewOutlivesOwner]: This view points into `owner`, which this function owns
  --> Tests/UI/Ownership/returned_trait_value_view_cannot_outlive_local_owner.jet:16:5
    |
 16 |     window
    |     ^^^^^^
 Why: `owner` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: Return an owned copy with `place.copy()` (for example `value[a..b].copy()`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305
